{"id": "20492424", "revid": "9784415", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20492424", "title": "Ren\u00e9 Dosi\u00e8re", "text": "Ren\u00e9 Dosi\u00e8re (born 3 August 1941) is a retired French politician and activist who served as a member of the National Assembly from 1988 to 1993 and again from 1997 until 2017. He represented the 1st constituency of the Aisne department, and was a member of the Socialiste, radical, citoyen et divers gauche group. He was a member of the national bureau of the Jeunesse Etudiante Chr\u00e9tienne between 1961 and 1962, in charge of high schools.\nBorn in Origny-Sainte-Benoite, Dosi\u00e8re is best known for his many questions to the government regarding the expenses of the services of the French presidency."}
